{"id":"mahabharata-1-200","work":"mahabharata","part":1,"partName":"आदिपर्व","partNameEn":"Adi Parva","unit":200,"title":"द्विशततमोऽध्यायः","titleEn":"Adhyaya 200 · Narada visits Indraprastha","summary":{"en":"The sage Narada comes to Indraprastha and is honoured by Yudhishthira and Draupadi. Fearing that the brothers might quarrel over their common wife, he offers to tell them an old story, and they ask to hear it.","kn":"ನಾರದರು ಇಂದ್ರಪ್ರಸ್ಥಕ್ಕೆ ಬಂದು ಯುಧಿಷ್ಠಿರ ದ್ರೌಪದಿಯರಿಂದ ಸನ್ಮಾನಿತರಾಗುತ್ತಾರೆ. ಸಾಮಾನ್ಯ ಪತ್ನಿಯ ವಿಷಯದಲ್ಲಿ ಸಹೋದರರು ಜಗಳವಾಡಬಹುದೆಂದು ಹೆದರಿ ಒಂದು ಹಳೆಯ ಕಥೆ ಹೇಳುವೆನೆನ್ನುತ್ತಾರೆ, ಅವರು ಕೇಳಲು ಬಯಸುತ್ತಾರೆ.","hi":"ऋषि नारद इन्द्रप्रस्थ आते हैं और युधिष्ठिर तथा द्रौपदी उनका सम्मान करते हैं। इस भय से कि भाई अपनी सामान्य पत्नी को लेकर झगड़ न पड़ें, वे एक पुरानी कथा सुनाने का प्रस्ताव करते हैं, और वे उसे सुनना चाहते हैं।","te":"నారదుడు ఇంద్రప్రస్థానికి వచ్చి యుధిష్ఠిర ద్రౌపదుల చేత సత్కరించబడతాడు. ఉమ్మడి భార్య విషయంలో సోదరులు కలహించవచ్చని భయపడి ఒక పాత కథ చెబుతానంటాడు, వారు వినగోరుతారు.","ta":"நாரதர் இந்திரப்ரஸ்தம் வந்து யுதிஷ்டிரராலும் திரௌபதியாலும் கௌரவிக்கப்படுகிறார். பொது மனைவி காரணமாகச் சகோதரர்கள் சண்டையிடக்கூடும் என்று அஞ்சி ஒரு பழங்கதையைச் சொல்ல முன்வர, அவர்கள் கேட்க விரும்புகிறார்கள்.","ml":"ഋഷി നാരദൻ ഇന്ദ്രപ്രസ്ഥത്തിൽ എത്തുന്നു; യുധിഷ്ഠിരനും ദ്രൗപദിയും അദ്ദേഹത്തെ ആദരിക്കുന്നു. പൊതുഭാര്യയെച്ചൊല്ലി സഹോദരന്മാർ കലഹിക്കുമോ എന്ന് ഭയന്ന അദ്ദേഹം ഒരു പുരാതന കഥ പറയാമെന്ന് വാഗ്ദാനം ചെയ്യുന്നു; അവർ കേൾക്കാൻ ആവശ്യപ്പെടുന്നു."},"source":"Mahabharata, Critical Edition (BORI, Pune) 1.200; e-text by M. Tokunaga and J. D. Smith, © BORI 1999, version of Thu Aug 22 2026","sections":[{"title":"अर्जुनवनवासपर्व","titleEn":"Arjunavanavasa Parva (Arjuna's forest exile)","verses":[{"text":"जनमेजय उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Janamejaya said:"}},{"n":1,"text":"एवं संप्राप्य राज्यं तदिन्द्रप्रस्थे तपोधन ।\nअत ऊर्ध्वं महात्मानः किमकुर्वन्त पाण्डवाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Having gained the kingdom at Indraprastha in this way, O ascetic, what did the great-souled Pandavas do after that?"}},{"n":2,"text":"सर्व एव महात्मानः पूर्वे मम पितामहाः ।\nद्रौपदी धर्मपत्नी च कथं तानन्ववर्तत ॥","meaning":{"en":"All of them, my great-souled forefathers, were so; how did Draupadi, their wife by dharma, conduct herself toward them?"}},{"n":3,"text":"कथं वा पञ्च कृष्णायामेकस्यां ते नराधिपाः ।\nवर्तमाना महाभागा नाभिद्यन्त परस्परम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"How was it that those five noble lords of men, living with the one Krishna, did not fall out with one another?"}},{"n":4,"text":"श्रोतुमिच्छाम्यहं सर्वं विस्तरेण तपोधन ।\nतेषां चेष्टितमन्योन्यं युक्तानां कृष्णया तया ॥","meaning":{"en":"I wish to hear it all in detail, O ascetic: how they behaved with one another, joined as they were with that Krishna."}},{"text":"वैशंपायन उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Vaishampayana said:"}},{"n":5,"text":"धृतराष्ट्राभ्यनुज्ञाताः कृष्णया सह पाण्डवाः ।\nरेमिरे पुरुषव्याघ्राः प्राप्तराज्याः परंतपाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Permitted by Dhritarashtra, the Pandavas, tigers among men and scourges of foes, having won their kingdom, took their pleasure there with Krishna."}},{"n":6,"text":"प्राप्य राज्यं महातेजाः सत्यसंधो युधिष्ठिरः ।\nपालयामास धर्मेण पृथिवीं भ्रातृभिः सह ॥","meaning":{"en":"Having gained the kingdom, the exceedingly radiant Yudhishthira, steadfast in his word, ruled the earth by dharma together with his brothers."}},{"n":7,"text":"जितारयो महाप्राज्ञाः सत्यधर्मपरायणाः ।\nमुदं परमिकां प्राप्तास्तत्रोषुः पाण्डुनन्दनाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Their enemies conquered, the very wise sons of Pandu, devoted to truth and dharma, dwelt there in supreme happiness."}},{"n":8,"text":"कुर्वाणाः पौरकार्याणि सर्वाणि पुरुषर्षभाः ।\nआसां चक्रुर्महार्हेषु पार्थिवेष्वासनेषु च ॥","meaning":{"en":"Those bulls among men attended to all the affairs of the city and sat on seats fit for great kings."}},{"n":9,"text":"अथ तेषूपविष्टेषु सर्वेष्वेव महात्मसु ।\nनारदस्त्वथ देवर्षिराजगाम यदृच्छया ।\nआसनं रुचिरं तस्मै प्रददौ स्वं युधिष्ठिरः ॥","meaning":{"en":"While all those great-souled men were seated, the divine sage Narada arrived of his own accord, and Yudhishthira gave him his own splendid seat."}},{"n":10,"text":"देवर्षेरुपविष्टस्य स्वयमर्घ्यं यथाविधि ।\nप्रादाद्युधिष्ठिरो धीमान्राज्यं चास्मै न्यवेदयत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"When the divine sage was seated, wise Yudhishthira himself offered him the guest-water according to rule, and presented his kingdom to him."}},{"n":11,"text":"प्रतिगृह्य तु तां पूजामृषिः प्रीतमनाभवत् ।\nआशीर्भिर्वर्धयित्वा तु तमुवाचास्यतामिति ॥","meaning":{"en":"The sage accepted that honor and was pleased; he blessed Yudhishthira and said, Please be seated."}},{"n":12,"text":"निषसादाभ्यनुज्ञातस्ततो राजा युधिष्ठिरः ।\nप्रेषयामास कृष्णायै भगवन्तमुपस्थितम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then King Yudhishthira sat down at his leave, and sent word to Krishna that the holy one had arrived."}},{"n":13,"text":"श्रुत्वैव द्रौपदी चापि शुचिर्भूत्वा समाहिता ।\nजगाम तत्र यत्रास्ते नारदः पाण्डवैः सह ॥","meaning":{"en":"On hearing it, Draupadi too, purified and composed, came to where Narada sat with the Pandavas."}},{"n":14,"text":"तस्याभिवाद्य चरणौ देवर्षेर्धर्मचारिणी ।\nकृताञ्जलिः सुसंवीता स्थिताथ द्रुपदात्मजा ॥","meaning":{"en":"The daughter of Drupada, steadfast in dharma, bowed at the feet of the divine sage and stood with joined palms, well covered."}},{"n":15,"text":"तस्याश्चापि स धर्मात्मा सत्यवागृषिसत्तमः ।\nआशिषो विविधाः प्रोच्य राजपुत्र्यास्तु नारदः ।\nगम्यतामिति होवाच भगवांस्तामनिन्दिताम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"The righteous sage Narada, truthful in speech, the best of seers, uttered many blessings on the king's daughter, and the holy one told the blameless woman to go."}},{"n":16,"text":"गतायामथ कृष्णायां युधिष्ठिरपुरोगमान् ।\nविविक्ते पाण्डवान्सर्वानुवाच भगवानृषिः ॥","meaning":{"en":"When Krishna had gone, the holy sage spoke privately to all the Pandavas, with Yudhishthira at their head."}},{"n":17,"text":"पाञ्चाली भवतामेका धर्मपत्नी यशस्विनी ।\nयथा वो नात्र भेदः स्यात्तथा नीतिर्विधीयताम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Panchali, the renowned, is the one wife by dharma of you all; so arrange the rule among yourselves that no division may arise among you."}},{"n":18,"text":"सुन्दोपसुन्दावसुरौ भ्रातरौ सहितावुभौ ।\nआस्तामवध्यावन्येषां त्रिषु लोकेषु विश्रुतौ ॥","meaning":{"en":"There were two brothers, the asuras Sunda and Upasunda, always together, famed in the three worlds as unslayable by anyone else."}},{"n":19,"text":"एकराज्यावेकगृहावेकशय्यासनाशनौ ।\nतिलोत्तमायास्तौ हेतोरन्योन्यमभिजघ्नतुः ॥","meaning":{"en":"They shared one kingdom, one house, one bed, one seat and one meal, yet because of Tilottama they killed each other."}},{"n":20,"text":"रक्ष्यतां सौहृदं तस्मादन्योन्यप्रतिभाविकम् ।\nयथा वो नात्र भेदः स्यात्तत्कुरुष्व युधिष्ठिर ॥","meaning":{"en":"Therefore guard your mutual affection, each bound to the other; do this, Yudhishthira, so that no division may arise among you."}},{"text":"युधिष्ठिर उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Yudhishthira said:"}},{"n":21,"text":"सुन्दोपसुन्दावसुरौ कस्य पुत्रौ महामुने ।\nउत्पन्नश्च कथं भेदः कथं चान्योन्यमघ्नताम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Great sage, whose sons were the asuras Sunda and Upasunda? How did the quarrel arise, and how did they kill each other?"}},{"n":22,"text":"अप्सरा देवकन्या वा कस्य चैषा तिलोत्तमा ।\nयस्याः कामेन संमत्तौ जघ्नतुस्तौ परस्परम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Whose child was this Tilottama, an apsara or a daughter of the gods, for desire of whom those two, maddened, struck each other down?"}},{"n":23,"text":"एतत्सर्वं यथावृत्तं विस्तरेण तपोधन ।\nश्रोतुमिच्छामहे विप्र परं कौतूहलं हि नः ॥","meaning":{"en":"We wish to hear all of this as it happened, in full, O ascetic Brahmin, for our curiosity is very great."}}]}]}